/T (For a process scheduler with frequent insertions and deletions, a red-black tree is a strong choice: it guarantees logarithmic operations while limiting rotations. The exact engineering decision should be confirmed by benchmarking the intended workload. A cached pointer to the leftmost node makes finding the minimum O\(1\); update the cached pointer when inserting a new minimum or deleting the current minimum.)
/E (For a process scheduler with frequent insertions and deletions, a red-black tree is a strong choice: it guarantees logarithmic operations while limiting rotations. The exact engineering decision should be confirmed by benchmarking the intended workload. A cached pointer to the leftmost node makes finding the minimum O\(1\); update the cached pointer when inserting a new minimum or deleting the current minimum.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [20]
>>
