/T (For a word or prefix of length m, trie search and prefix counting take O\(m\), independent of the total number of stored words \(assuming constant-time child indexing\). Inserting a contact takes O\(m\). A 26-pointer array at every node wastes space for sparse branches. A compressed trie/radix tree merges single-child paths into string labels, reducing the number of nodes and pointer overhead.)
/E (For a word or prefix of length m, trie search and prefix counting take O\(m\), independent of the total number of stored words \(assuming constant-time child indexing\). Inserting a contact takes O\(m\). A 26-pointer array at every node wastes space for sparse branches. A compressed trie/radix tree merges single-child paths into string labels, reducing the number of nodes and pointer overhead.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
