/T (The hybrid is selected because the trie/radix tree handles character-prefix operations efficiently, while the sorted array handles alphabetical range queries simply and efficiently. At 2 million words, use a memory-mapped or disk-backed sorted index, compress trie edges and store compact integer references. One remaining limitation is spell-check: edit-distance suggestions can visit many trie states and need careful pruning and a latency limit.)
/E (The hybrid is selected because the trie/radix tree handles character-prefix operations efficiently, while the sorted array handles alphabetical range queries simply and efficiently. At 2 million words, use a memory-mapped or disk-backed sorted index, compress trie edges and store compact integer references. One remaining limitation is spell-check: edit-distance suggestions can visit many trie states and need careful pruning and a latency limit.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
