/T (A hash table provides O\(1\) average exact lookup; a sorted array provides O\(log n + k\) range listing and prefix listing using two binary searches. Autocomplete finds the first and last matching positions and returns the interval. Spell-check still needs an additional candidate-generation method. The total space is O\(n\) references plus stored words, but the same word is indexed twice. Weekly updates must update both structures; rebuilding the sorted array in a batch is often simpler than inserting each word with O\(n\) shifting.)
/E (A hash table provides O\(1\) average exact lookup; a sorted array provides O\(log n + k\) range listing and prefix listing using two binary searches. Autocomplete finds the first and last matching positions and returns the interval. Spell-check still needs an additional candidate-generation method. The total space is O\(n\) references plus stored words, but the same word is indexed twice. Weekly updates must update both structures; rebuilding the sorted array in a batch is often simpler than inserting each word with O\(n\) shifting.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
