929 0 obj
<<
/Title (A hash table provides O\(1\) average exact lookup; a sorted array provides O\(log n + k\) range listing and prefix listing using two binary searches. Autocomplete finds the first and last matching positions and returns the interval. Spell-check still needs an additional candidate-generation method. The total space is O\(n\) references plus stored words, but the same word is indexed twice. Weekly updates must update both structures; rebuilding the sorted array in a batch is often simpler than inserting each word with O\(n\) shifting.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 741 0 R
/First 1020 0 R
/Last 1021 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
